# jc-nvim Key Reference *jc-ref*
[Course](@tutor:jc-nvim) | [Safety](*jc-ref-safety*) | [Sources](*jc-ref-sources*)

Scope: all personalized mappings and common effective defaults, not every
native Vim or optional plugin command. This is a reference, not a drill sheet.
Leader and localleader are Space. `Space sf` means Space, s, f in sequence.
Modes: n Normal; i Insert; x Visual; s Select; o operator-pending; c command-line;
t terminal-input; v means both Visual and Select for shared custom mappings.
`<C-...>` is Ctrl; `<S-...>` Shift; `<M-...>` Alt/Meta. Case matters.
Buffer-local UI mappings override globals. Availability depends on filetype/server.
In native Tutor, Enter/double-click follow links; do not use its >> command injection on reference text.

## Safety and Known Limits *jc-ref-safety*
- Visual Shift-Left/Right can DELETE selected text at line boundaries; avoid edges.
- Netrw Tab/Shift-Tab set Vim marks f/F, not file marks: nonrecursive RHS mf/mF.
- Terminal `<C-\>` navigates away, intercepting native `<C-\><C-n>` terminal escape.
- Default navigator `<C-h/j/k/l>` mappings are DISABLED; use Ctrl-Arrows instead.
- Surround `ds`, `cs`, Visual `S`, and other defaults are disabled; see [surround](*jc-ref-surround*).
- Git mutations, Mason changes, plugin updates and history rewrites are reference-only, never drills.
- AI, server, filesystem and Git exercises require suitable buffers or disposable projects.
- Terminal protocols can alias Tab/Ctrl-I or intercept Ctrl-S/Alt keys; test actual input.

## Core Editing and Navigation *jc-ref-core*
- n `Space R`: restart Neovim. n `Space ps`: `vim.pack.update()`; reference-only.
- n `Space e`: Explore current file's directory and focus its entry; netrw uses Rexplore.
- n `<Home>` / `<End>`: previous/next tracked file, centered; counts work, e.g. `3<Home>`.
- File history tracks named, listed ordinary buffers, not cursor positions or special UIs.
- v `<S-Up>` / `<S-Down>`: move selected rows up/down, reindent and reselect.
- v `<S-Left>` / `<S-Right>`: characterwise region move using register s; unsafe at edges.
- n `>` / `<`: indent/unindent current line; NOT the native motion-taking operators.
- v `>` / `<`: indent/unindent and retain selection.
- n `J`: join two lines and restore cursor via mark z; `3J` still joins only two lines.
- n/v `<PageDown>` / `<PageUp>`: half-page down/up, then center.
- n `n` / `N`: repeat search forward/backward relative to search direction, center and unfold.
- c `<CR>`: accept `/` or `?` search, center and unfold; other commands get ordinary Enter.
- n `<Esc>`: clear search highlighting; also clears a pending Sidekick next edit.
- n `Space r`: whole-file, whole-word, case-sensitive replacement prompt for cursor word.
- The replacement starts EMPTY: accepting immediately deletes matches; netrw overrides this key.
- v `p`: black-hole delete selection then P; preserve the previous yank for repeated replacement.
- n/v `d`, `D`, `c`, `C`: delete/change through black-hole register, preserving previous yank.
- n `D`/`C`: to line end; character/line Visual D/C affect whole lines; block Visual D/C extend each row to EOL.
- i `<C-c>`: Escape, including normal InsertLeave behavior.
- n `Space n` / `Space p`: next/previous LOCATION-list item and center, not quickfix.
- n `Space q`: close open location list, or populate/open current-buffer diagnostics there.
- n/v/i/t `<C-Left/Down/Up/Right>`: neighboring split or tmux pane in that direction.
- n/v/i/t `<C-\>`: previous split/pane. Do not use it as terminal escape in this setup.
- Native basics: `u` undo, `<C-r>` redo, `.` repeat; black-hole deletion means `dd` does not copy.
- Native folds: `zo` open, `zc` close, `za` toggle, `zR` open all, `zM` close all.
- Native comments: n `gcc` line, `gc{motion}` region; x `gc` selection. Not commentary.
- Help: [registers](registers), [location lists](location-list), [folds](fold-commands), [comments](gc).

## LSP and Runtime Defaults *jc-ref-lsp*
- Attached-buffer n `grn`: rename; n/x `gra`: code action.
- Attached-buffer n `grr`: Telescope references; `gri`: implementations.
- Attached-buffer n `grd`: definitions, NOT `gd`; `grD`: declaration.
- Attached-buffer n `grt`: type definitions; `gO`: document symbols.
- Attached-buffer n `gW`: dynamic workspace symbols; picker i `<C-Space>` fuzzy-refines results.
- Attached-buffer n `Space th`: toggle this buffer's inlay hints, only when supported.
- Runtime n `K`: hover when available; `grx`: codelens action when supported.
- Runtime n `]d` / `[d`: next/previous diagnostic; `]D` / `[D`: last/first diagnostic.
- Runtime n `<C-w>d` or `<C-w><C-d>`: diagnostic float.
- Runtime i/s `<C-s>`: signature help; Copilot overrides INSERT Ctrl-S with word acceptance.
- Runtime x/o `an` / `in`: parent/child syntax-node selection, with parser or LSP selection-range support.
- Server operations need an attached supporting server; plain Tutor buffers may have none.
- n `Space f`: Conform asynchronous WHOLE-buffer format, with LSP fallback; not a range key.
- Saving autoformats with a 500 ms timeout/LSP fallback, except C/C++ skip format-on-save.
- Formatters: stylua, phpcbf, gofumpt + goimports, rustfmt, shfmt, black, prettierd by filetype.
- Help: [LSP defaults](lsp-defaults), [diagnostics](diagnostic-defaults), [formatting](conform).

## Telescope Launchers *jc-ref-search*
All are Normal mode; picker controls are [below](*jc-ref-picker*).
- `Space sh`: help tags; `Space sk`: keymaps.
- `Space sf`: files; `Space sp`: Git-tracked project files.
- `Space sn`: Fidget notifications; `Space st`: Telescope builtin picker list.
- `Space sw`: grep cursor word; `Space sg`: live grep.
- `Space sd`: diagnostics; `Space sr`: resume last picker.
- `Space s.`: recent files; `Space Space`: buffers.
- `Space /`: fuzzy search current buffer, dropdown without preview.
- `Space s/`: live grep restricted to open files.
- `Space sc`: files under this Neovim configuration directory.
- When startup cwd basename is dotfiles, file/grep pickers include hidden files.
- Live grep/word grep require rg; local search does not need an online service.
- Telescope also handles vim.ui.select choices, including code-action/prompt menus.

## Telescope Picker Controls *jc-ref-picker*
- i type: filter; i `<Esc>`: Normal mode; n `<Esc>` or i `<C-c>`: close.
- i `<C-n>`/`<C-p>`, i/n `<Down>`/`<Up>`, n `j`/`k`: next/previous result.
- n `H`/`M`/`L`: top/middle/bottom; `gg`/`G`: first/last result.
- i/n `<CR>`: choose; `<C-x>` split, `<C-v>` vsplit, `<C-t>` tab, unless picker overrides.
- i/n `<Tab>`/`<S-Tab>`: toggle multi-selection and move to worse/better-ranked result.
- i/n `<C-u>`/`<C-d>`: preview up/down; `<C-f>`/`<C-k>`: preview left/right.
- i/n `<PageUp>`/`<PageDown>`: results up/down; `<M-f>`/`<M-k>`: results left/right.
- i/n `<C-q>`: ALL results to quickfix, replacing list; `<M-q>`: multi-selected results only.
- i `<C-/>` or `<C-_>`, n `?`: toggle key help; no separate which-key plugin needed.
- i `<C-l>`: prefilter-tag completion, only supported by some pickers; not surround.
- i `<C-w>`: delete preceding word; `<C-j>`: NO-OP, not next result.
- i `<C-r><C-w/a/f/l>`: insert original word/WORD/filename/line respectively.
- i/n left click selects; double-left click performs default action.
- Buffer picker i/n `<M-d>`: delete buffer(s); cached-pickers i/n `<C-x>`: remove cached picker.
- Command/search history i/n `<C-e>`: edit entry; registers `<CR>` paste, `<C-e>` edit.
- Quickfix-history i/n `<C-q>`: activate/open chosen historical list.
- Live-grep i `<C-Space>`: fuzzy-refine collected results; not Flash/Blink here.
- Fidget `<CR>` echoes chosen notification and closes; `<C-x/v/t>` only close.
- vim.ui.select `<CR>` chooses; closing cancels. Blink normally stays disabled in prompt buffers.
- No configured history-cycle or previewer-cycle shortcuts. [Picker help](telescope.mappings).

## Harpoon Files *jc-ref-harpoon*
- n `Space ma`: add current file; `Space mf`: toggle native quick menu.
- n `<M-1>` through `<M-9>`: select corresponding file in current cwd's Harpoon list.
- Quick-menu n `<CR>`: resolve edited list, close and open current row.
- Quick-menu n `q`/`<Esc>`: save/close; `:w` saves/closes; leaving buffer also saves/closes.
- Menu is editable: `j/k`, `gg/G`, `{count}G` navigate; edit/delete rows to change bookmarks.
- Global black-hole `d` applies: menu `dd` deletes a bookmark WITHOUT copying it.
- To reorder, use `yy`, then `dd`, move, then `P`; or use [:move](:move). NOT `dd` then `p`.
- Direct menu digits 1-9 are NOT enabled; no native-menu split/vsplit shortcuts configured.
- Optional Telescope Harpoon extension is separate, not explicitly loaded by this config.
- Its i/n `<C-d>` prompts to delete current/selected marks: y + Enter confirms.
- Its i/n `<C-p>` moves item to list index +1; `<C-n>` to index -1, NOT cursor navigation.
- Filtered/sorted indices make that reorder unreliable; use arrows to navigate this picker.
- Native menu saves on toggle and syncs to disk; current-file highlight adds no keys.

## Netrw Files *jc-ref-netrw*
All keys below are Normal mode in a netrw buffer. [Netrw help](netrw-quickmap).
- `Space e`: Rexplore toggle; `<C-c>`: delete/close browser buffer.
- `<C-h>`: native jumplist back then center; `<C-l>`: forward then center, bypassing Sidekick.
- `Space r`: refresh via e!, NOT global word replacement.
- `N`: filename prompt, create missing parent directories; refuses to overwrite existing files.
- BROKEN intended shortcuts: `<Tab>` -> literal mf, `<S-Tab>` -> literal mF, nonrecursively.
- They set Vim marks f/F. Use literal `mf` and `mF` for netrw file marking/unmarking.
- The custom FileType hook binds these maps; icons/parsing target thin/long/tree listings, not wide style.
- `<CR>`: enter directory/open file; `-`: parent directory.
- `o`/`v`/`t`: horizontal split/vsplit/tab; `p`: preview; `P`: open in previous window.
- `u`/`U`: previous/next directory history, NOT the editor jumplist.
- `%`: new file; `d`: new directory; `R`: rename; `D`/`<Del>`: delete (filesystem changes).
- `mf`: toggle file mark; `mF`: clear listing marks; `mu`: clear all file marks.
- `mt`: set target directory; `mc`/`mm`: copy/move marked files there (filesystem changes).
- `mr`: mark by pattern; `me`: edit marked files; `md`: diff marked files.
- `mb`/`gb`/`qb`: bookmark/go to previous bookmark/list bookmarks and history.
- `gh`: toggle dotfiles; `a`: cycle hiding rules; `i`: listing style; `I`: banner.
- `s`: sorting criterion, NOT surround; `r`: reverse sorting; `S`: sort sequence.
- `cd`: change cwd; `gn`: tree root; `qf`: file information; `<F1>`: help.
- `x`: associated external program; `X`: execute filename. Reference-only, not navigation drills.
- Default Ctrl-H hide-list editing and Ctrl-L refresh are replaced by custom history keys.

## Blink Completion *jc-ref-blink*
Default preset, NOT super-tab/enter. [Keymap help](blink-cmp-config-keymap).
- i `<C-Space>`: show completion, then show/hide documentation as applicable.
- i `<C-y>`: select/accept current or first completion; this is the completion accept key.
- i `<C-e>`: CANCEL completion, undo insertion preview; then fallback if not handled.
- i `<Up>`/`<Down>`: previous/next completion, else fallback.
- i `<C-p>`/`<C-n>`: previous/next, else other mappings ONLY, not native completion.
- i `<C-b>`: documentation up four lines, else fallback.
- i `<C-f>`: accept visible Copilot suggestion, else documentation down, else fallback.
- i `<Tab>`: next snippet placeholder -> Sidekick next edit jump/apply -> tabout/native fallback.
- i `<S-Tab>`: previous snippet placeholder -> tabout fallback.
- i `<C-k>`: show/hide signature help, else fallback.
- s `<Tab>`/`<S-Tab>`: snippet forward/backward; Tab also tries Sidekick; Select-mode fallback.
- s `<C-k>`: signature; s `<C-f>`: Copilot callback then fallback, NO documentation scrolling.
- Insert Enter and Tab do NOT accept Blink completions; Enter is autopairs-aware newline.
- Preselection/insertion preview default on; documentation auto-opens after 200 ms.
- Sources: LSP, paths, snippets, buffer, LazyDev; Copilot is separate ghost text, not a source.
- c `<Tab>`: show/insert first or accept sole item, then next; `<S-Tab>` starts last/goes previous.
- c `<C-n>`/`<Right>` and `<C-p>`/`<Left>`: next/previous completion, else native fallback.
- c `<C-Space>` show; `<C-y>` select/accept; `<C-e>` cancel; `<End>` hide then native End.
- Command-line auto-show is enabled; Insert Ctrl-F/Tab overrides do not apply there.
- Blink wraps mappings on InsertEnter; prompt buffers/macros disable it; terminal completion is off.

## Copilot and Next Edits *jc-ref-ai*
- Copilot-attached i `<C-d>`: accept suggestion line; `<C-s>`: accept word, else previous/native key.
- Copilot-attached i `<C-g>`: next/request suggestion, NO fallback to native Ctrl-G prefix.
- i `<C-f>`: full visible suggestion acceptance through Blink, before documentation scrolling.
- Suggestions auto-trigger; accept keys do not request suggestions when none are visible.
- Blink menu open hides Copilot ghost text; close unhides it. Ctrl-F then normally scrolls docs.
- No standalone accept/previous/dismiss/toggle key; Copilot panel and its Alt-Enter key are disabled.
- Copilot's own NES is off, but Sidekick NES is ON; n `<C-i>` jumps to/applies the next edit.
- n `<C-i>` falls back to native forward jumplist if no edit; Sidekick adds no jumplist entry.
- `<Esc>` clears NES; entering Insert or changing text in Insert also clears it.
- Tutor/special buffers need not support AI; Copilot excludes Markdown/YAML/help/commit filetypes.
- Copilot requires network, authentication/access, attached server, curl and Node.js 22+.
- Sidekick NES needs Copilot inline-edit server support; CLI tools are separate optional services.
- Help: [Copilot](copilot.txt), [Sidekick](sidekick.nvim.txt). No unconfigured CLI launchers listed.

## Surround Inputs *jc-ref-surround*
- n `s{motion}{delimiter}`: add surround, e.g. `siw)`; replaces native substitute-character s.
- i `<C-l>{delimiter}`: pair around cursor; `<C-l><C-l>{delimiter}`: delimiters on new lines.
- Double Ctrl-L is NOT an existing-whole-line surround; single Ctrl-L can wait for its prefix.
- Disabled n keys: `ys`, `yss`, `yS`, `ySS`, `ds`, `cs`, `cS`; no delete/change-surround shortcut.
- Disabled i keys: `<C-g>s`, `<C-g>S`; disabled x keys: `S`, `gS`.
- `(`, `[`, `{`, `<`: paired delimiters with interior spaces; `)`, `]`, `}`, `>`: without spaces.
- Single quote, double quote, backtick: matching quotes; `a/b/B/r` alias `>/)/}/]` respectively.
- `t`/`T`: prompt for HTML tag/attributes; `f`: function-name prompt; `i`: left/right delimiter prompts.
- Enter accepts prompts; Esc/Ctrl-C cancel. Other printable delimiters repeat on both sides.
- q/s search aliases are not generic add aliases. [Surround help](nvim-surround.txt).
~~~
siw)    surround current word with tight parentheses
siw(    surround current word with spaced parentheses
~~~

## Syntax Textobjects *jc-ref-objects*
- x/o `af`/`if`: outer/inner function; `ac`/`ic`: class; `aa`/`ia`: parameter.
- x/o `as`: local scope from @local.scope in the locals query group.
- n/x/o `[f`/`]f`: previous/next function START; `[c`/`]c`: previous/next class START.
- Lookahead is on; outer selections include surrounding whitespace.
- af is LINEWISE, ac is BLOCKWISE, aa is characterwise; these choices affect operators.
- Motions do not add jumplist entries. No end-motion/swap/repeat mappings configured.
- Parser and matching language queries required; folds start open at foldlevel 99.
- Help: [textobjects](nvim-treesitter-textobjects), [native nodes](treesitter).

## Flash Inputs *jc-ref-flash*
- n/x/o `zk`: text jump; `zt`: Treesitter range; `<C-Space>`: incremental Treesitter selection.
- x/o `zr`: remote motion/operation and restore location; `zs`: Treesitter search/range.
- n/x/o `f/F/t/T` and `;/,`: Flash-enhanced character motions/repeats, multiline by default.
- `/` and `?` also show Flash labels; no configured command-line toggle key.
- General labels: arstgmneioqwfpbjluyzxcdvkh, plus uppercase labels when needed.
- Treesitter zt/Ctrl-Space labels instead use abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz.
- Inside UI: type pattern then displayed label; Enter chooses current target; Esc cancels.
- Search Backspace removes pattern text; Treesitter `;` expands, `,` contracts.
- Incremental selection additionally uses Ctrl-Space to expand, Backspace to contract.
- Character UI `;`/`,` repeat original/opposite direction; lower/uppercase motion keys also repeat.
- Character labels exclude hjkliardc and are suppressed for counts/macros.
- n zt no longer means scroll-to-top; n zk no longer means previous spelling error.
- Only Blink menu/documentation/signature filetypes are explicitly excluded. [Flash help](flash.nvim.txt).

## Autopairs and Tabout *jc-ref-pairs*
- i opening parentheses/brackets/braces/quotes/backticks insert matching closers when context permits.
- i existing closer skips over it; Backspace deletes empty pair; Enter adds pair-aware newline.
- Defaults also handle markup comments, fences, triple quotes and newlines between markup tags.
- Treesitter checking is on; autopairs is disabled in TelescopePrompt, macros and Replace mode.
- No autopairs Ctrl-H/Ctrl-W or fast-wrap key is enabled.
- After Blink fallback, Tab moves out through quotes/backticks or ()[]{}; otherwise ordinary Tab.
- Shift-Tab moves backward; if impossible it does NOTHING, not outdent. Parser support required.

## Git Reference Only *jc-ref-git*
- n `Space gf`: Fugitive status. [Status/action help](fugitive-maps). Use disposable repositories.
- Global n `y<C-g>`: yank Fugitive-object path; c `<C-r><C-g>`: insert escaped object path.
- Status n/x `s`/`u`/`-`: stage/unstage/toggle; n `U`: unstage all; n/x `=`/`>`/`<`: toggle/show/hide diff.
- Status n/x `X` discards changes; `2X`/`3X` ours/theirs. These are NOT text-editor undo operations.
- Status n `<CR>`/`o`/`gO`/`O`/`1p`: open/split/vsplit/tab/preview; `gq` closes; `g?`/`<F1>` help.
- n `dd`, `dh`/`ds`, `dv`: default/horizontal/vertical diff; `dq` closes other diffs; n/x `I`/`P` patch.
- n/x/o `(`/`)`: items; `[c`/`]c` or `K`/`J`: hunks; `[m`/`]m` or `[/`/`]/`: files.
- n/x/o `[[`/`]]`: section starts; `[]`/`][`: ends; `gu/gU/gs/gp/gP/gr`: status sections.
- Status n `i`: next expanded hunk; n/x `gI`: add ignore entry; `.`: command line with current paths.
- n `cc`/`cvc`: commit; `ca/cva/ce/cw`: amend/reword; `cf/cF/cs/cS/cn/cW`: fixup/squash, reference-only.
- Stash/revert/checkout/rebase families `cz/cr/co/r` mutate files/history; read help, do not drill.
- Fugitive `s`, `cs`, `gc`, `[c`/`]c` have Git meanings, overriding surround/comments/class navigation.
- Three-way diff `d2o`/`d3o` obtain ours/theirs hunks. [Diff help](:Gdiffsplit!).
- Git Telescope i/n: status `<Tab>` stages; commits `<CR>` checks out; `<C-r>m/s/h` reset mixed/soft/HARD.
- Git branches i/n `<CR>` checkout; `<C-t/r/a/s/d/y>` track/rebase/create/switch/delete/merge.
- Git stash `<CR>` applies; buffer-commits `<CR>` checkout file revision, `<C-x/v/t>` revision diffs.
- Gitsigns adds NO custom/global hunk keys here; commentary and unimpaired are not installed.

## Optional UIs and Sources *jc-ref-sources*
- Command-only `:Glow`: preview n `q`/`<Esc>` close, normal scrolling; local glow needed. [Help](glow.nvim.txt).
- `:ConformInfo`: n `q`/`<C-c>` close. Gitsigns focused popup n `q` closes. [Gitsigns help](gitsigns).
- Gitsigns blame n `<CR>` menu; `r`/`R` reblame commit/parent; `d` diff tab; `s/S/e` show vsplit/tab/current.
- `:Mason`: n `<CR>` details/log, `g?` help, `<C-f>` filter, `1-5` views, `q`/`<Esc>` close/clear state.
- Mason n `i/u/U/X` install/update/all/uninstall; `c/C` versions; `<C-c>` cancel: reference-only. [Help](mason.nvim).
- Optional Sidekick CLI-local n/t `<C-b>`/`<C-f>` pick context, `<C-.>` hide, `<C-z>` previous window.
- CLI n `q`/`<C-q>` hide; t `<C-q>` Normal mode, `<C-p>` prompt; n `<CR>` enters terminal-input and sends Enter.
- CLI t `<C-h/j/k/l>` navigate windows or pass through; not global navigator defaults.
- Sidekick falls back to Telescope context picking; its `<CR>` sends context instead of opening files.
- No prescribed terminal-exit drill. CLI tools require separate installation/authentication. [Help](sidekick.nvim.txt).
- Sources: lua/user/keymaps.lua, lsp.lua, plugins.lua; Neovim 0.12.5 runtime docs; installed plugin code.
